# IR Definition

- `IRDefinition` is the **SSOT (Single Source Of Truth)**. Treat breaking changes as high-risk; prefer additive changes. An IR schema migration *engine* is deferred (distinct from snapshot *product* versions under `versions/`).
- Projection views (e.g. map by `logicalId`) are not IR. Do not persist them on the snapshot or import adapter types here. See `.cursor/rules/16-plugins.mdc`.
- Keep this package free of external UI-framework types, file I/O, and Svelte.
- Concrete UI kinds live under `src/lib/ir/elements/` and **extend** `Component`.
- `IRDefinition` aggregates elements; it does not know about Reader/Writer/Raw schemas.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — domain-only
export class Button extends Component { ... }

// ❌ BAD — framework leak into IR
import type { SomethingFromVendorSdk } from 'vendor-ui';
```
